# Arithmetic assembly identities for the bcs coordination sequence

The per-class level-set counts of the bcs distance functions sum to 6n²+2:
on even shells the count is class 1 + three copies of the 5/6/7 family; on odd
shells it is four copies of the 2/3/4/8 family. Both identities are stated with
explicit parity witnesses so no natural-number division appears anywhere.
